module BigListNorm

(* Regression test for issue #4394: reducing a recursive function over a large
   list with the normalizer used to take time quadratic in the length of the
   list. The cause was that weakly reducing a `match` scrutinee (the
   `weakly_reduce_scrutinee` step) rejected, and therefore recomputed from
   scratch, all the memoized normal forms taken by the enclosing strong
   normalization. See `cfg_equivalent` in FStarC.TypeChecker.Normalize.

   The Makefile checks this file within a time limit. *)

open FStar.UInt8

